Why GPLv3-or-later, recorded so nobody has to re-derive it:

  - It matches the ecosystem this tool exists to serve. Moodle core is GPLv3,
    ucl-isd/moodle is GPL-3.0, and ucl-isd/moodle-mod_coursework carries GPLv3
    headers. Every consumer of this action is a Moodle plugin repository, which
    is GPLv3+ by convention.
  - It removes a real friction: this repo reads and vendors Moodle-produced
    artifacts (backup .mbz fixtures, lib/plugins.json data). Under a permissive
    licence, copying any of those in raised a licence-mixing question every
    time. Under the same licence as Moodle, it does not.
  - The sole dependency, Playwright, is Apache-2.0, which is compatible in this
    direction (Apache-2.0 code may be combined into a GPLv3 work).

It was MIT until 2026-08-09 only because the initial scaffold commit
(7834104) included an MIT template. Nothing in the repo relied on it: no gate
check, no test, no dependency, and it is not published to the GitHub
Marketplace.

